Plunkr of your case: http://plnkr.co/edit/x3YCwSqzzMeHcx2RVDyp?p=preview

With FormsDeprecated it was possible via `ngControl` + `ControlGroup`

``` twig
<form [ngFormModel]="type.control">
    <select class="form-control" ngControl="country">
        <option [ngValue]="null">Please select value</option>
        <option *ngFor="let country of countries" [ngValue]="country.value">{{ country.label }}</option>
    </select>
</form>
```

``` typescript
import {ControlGroup, Control} from '@angular/common';

    // ...
    public control = new ControlGroup({
        country: new Control(null)
    });
    // ...
```

Don't know about the new forms - or in your case - without ngForms, through.
